# The comparison bench on ECP5. Only `clk` is located, and to soc/littlesoc.lpf's
# own SITE "P3" -- the pad that file's header records as the one that mattered,
# because the pad decides where the global network is entered. The two LEDs are
# left to `--lpf-allow-unconstrained` the way the SoC's own flow leaves its
# unconstrained pins: a placed LED pad is not part of what this measures, and
# inventing sites for them would put two made-up numbers in a timing report.
#
# ECP5's clock is CONTINUOUS -- no SB_HFOSC step function -- so a frequency here
# is a frequency, and a core's critical-path advantage is one it can spend. That
# is why the comparison runs on two parts: up5k answers "what is fastest on the
# board this ships to", and this answers "what is architecturally faster when the
# clock is yours to choose".
LOCATE COMP "clk" SITE "P3";
IOBUF PORT "clk" IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33;
